  "At easier levels, move slowly until you learn the movement.": "På lettere niveauer skal du bevæge dig langsomt, indtil du lærer bevægelsen.",
  "At least 120 min of scheduled Zone 2 and about 51 min of hard cardio a week; controlled vigorous blocks on Tuesday, Thursday and Saturday.": "Mindst 120 min planlagt zone 2 og ca. 51 min hård cardio om ugen; kontrollerede kraftige blokke tirsdag, torsdag og lørdag.",
  "At New to training and Returning, keep the pace brisk and below all-out effort. At Active, work hard. At Well trained, use all-out effort.": "At New to training and Returning, hold tempoet højt og under den største indsats. At Active, arbejd hårdt. At Well trained, brug en total indsats.",
  "At Returning and above, hold a dumbbell in each hand, or loop a band around your waist with its anchor in front of you. The band should pull you forward, like a sled.": "At Returning and above, hold en håndvægt i hver hånd, eller sløj et bånd rundt om din talje med dets anker foran dig. Båndet skal trække dig frem, som en slæde.",
  "At Returning, push back up with your hands. At higher levels, pull yourself back with your hamstrings.": "At Returning, skub op igen med dine hænder. At higher levels, træk dig selv tilbage med dine baglår.",
  "At the end of your last interval, note your peak heart rate. Walk gently for 60 seconds and note your heart rate again. Enter the drop (peak minus 60s reading).": "I slutningen af ​​dit sidste interval skal du notere din maksimale puls. Gå forsigtigt i 60 sekunder og noter din puls igen. Indtast faldet (peak minus 60s læsning).",
